; Open struct-map IGNORE flavor (`@ignore` on the rest row) end-to-end round-trip vectors. `@ignore`
; tolerate-and-DROPS unknown map entries: each is typed-deserialized (key AND value, so the stream
; advances correctly) and then discarded — no `rest` field, and serialize re-emits ONLY the declared
; members. Non-preserve only (`@ignore` is rejected under --preserve-encodings). The `any` value
; range still exercises the AnyCbor skip primitive (drop-through of arbitrary CBOR). Every `wire`
; byte string in tests.rs is hand-written from the CBOR grammar, not copied from generator output.
; (The `; @ignore` comment must precede the closing `}` on its own line — a CDDL comment runs to the
; end of the line, so `; @ignore }` would swallow the brace.)
foo = {
  1: uint, 2: text,
  * uint => any ; @ignore
}
bar = {
  ? 3: text,
  * uint => any ; @ignore
}
baz = {
  1: uint,
  * any => any ; @ignore
}
